{"id":"n4-044","title":"Verb てしまう","romaji":"〜te shimau","jlptLevel":4,"shortExplanation":"Expresses unintentional actions or actions with regrettable outcomes; 'to end up doing', 'to accidentally do'.","longExplanation":"The ～てしまう grammar point is used to indicate unintentional actions or actions with regrettable outcomes. It can often be translated as 'to end up doing' or 'to accidentally do' in English. The formation requires adding しまう to the て-form of a verb.","formation":"Verb-te form + しまう","examples":[{"jp":"ケーキを全部食べてしまった。","romaji":"Keeki wo zenbu tabete shimatta.","en":"I ended up eating the whole cake.","words":[{"surface":"ケーキ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"全部","vocabId":"1396130","reading":"ぜんぶ"},{"surface":"食べ","vocabId":"1358280","reading":"たべる","baseForm":"食べる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"しまっ","vocabId":"1305380","reading":"しまう","baseForm":"しまう"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5]},{"jp":"宿題を忘れてしまいました。","romaji":"Shukudai wo wasurete shimaimashita.","en":"I accidentally forgot my homework.","words":[{"surface":"宿題","vocabId":"1337270","reading":"しゅくだい"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"忘れ","vocabId":"1519210","reading":"わすれる","baseForm":"忘れる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"しまい","vocabId":"1305380","reading":"しまう","baseForm":"しまう"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"彼に秘密を言ってしまった。","romaji":"Kare ni himitsu wo itte shimatta.","en":"I accidentally told him the secret.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"秘密","vocabId":"1484150","reading":"ひみつ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"言っ","vocabId":"1587040","reading":"いう","baseForm":"言う"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"しまっ","vocabId":"1305380","reading":"しまう","baseForm":"しまう"},{"surface":"た","voca